# Vallaki's townsfolk about their day (lane 4, F2): Goodwife Marta on her morning round of the market row and the main
# street, Old Kolya hauling festival wicker from the lower town, and Ilie lighting the lamps after dark. They walk
# their routes (the location's `path`) and stop when someone comes up to them.

~ goodwife
if flag.festival_over and flag.vallaki_backed == "neither"
Goodwife Marta [smile]: No festival this week. Nobody's said we may stop smiling, but nobody's checking either. I'd forgotten what my own face does.
-> END
endif
if flag.festival_begun and not flag.festival_over
Goodwife Marta: Off to the square with you. They count the faces, you know. Mine's been counted. I'm only fetching bread.
-> END
endif
Goodwife Marta [smile]: Good morning! It is a good morning. The Baron says so, and the Baron's men are standing right over there, so it is.
* How is the market? -> market
* Heard anything interesting? -> marta_rumor
* Good morning to you. -> END

~ marta_rumor
Goodwife Marta: Interesting? In Vallaki? Blinsky, I suppose. The toymaker. He asks every stranger who comes through the gate if they've been up the hill to the castle.
Goodwife Marta: Not about the count. About a toy. Some jester his old master made up there, that walked about on its own. He wants to know if it still walks. Poor man.
if not quest.toymakers_masterpiece
quest toymakers_masterpiece rumored
endif
interject tag:curious: A toy that walks. In that castle. I'd like to know too.
-> END

~ market
Goodwife Marta: Turnips, mostly. Turnips and Blinsky's toys, which nobody buys, and the Baron's festival bunting, which everybody buys, because it's noticed who doesn't.
interject tag:blunt: So the bunting's a tax.
Goodwife Marta: Hush. It's a celebration.
-> END

~ carter
if flag.festival_over
Old Kolya: No more wicker to haul. My back thanks you, whoever you are. My purse doesn't.
-> END
endif
Old Kolya: Mind the cart. That's a sun, that is. Will be. Every week I bring the wicker up, every week they burn it, every week the sky stays grey.
Old Kolya: Don't tell the Baron I said "grey".
-> END

~ lamplighter
if quest.black_roses and quest.black_roses != rumored
-> vallaki/black_roses:ilie
endif
Ilie the Lamplighter: Evening. Every lamp lit by the last bell, or I answer for it. The Baron says a lit street is a happy street.
if guest:ireena
Ilie the Lamplighter: Your friend should keep her hood up. The dark has eyes on this town, and some of them are at the windows.
endif
* Who are the lamps really for? -> lamplighter_ana
* [if flag.roses_rumor] There were black roses on the chandler's step this morning. -> vallaki/black_roses:asks
* Good evening. -> END

~ lamplighter_ana
Ilie the Lamplighter: For my girl, Ana. Last winter she slept with her window open a crack, for the stove smoke. Three mornings later the watch found her at the lake gate, sitting against the post, smiling, white as milk.
Ilie the Lamplighter [sad]: The Baron called it a chill. The next day there were black roses on our step, and a card in a very fine hand: "With sympathy, from her neighbour across the lake."
interject tag:blunt: He sent flowers. To her father.
Ilie the Lamplighter: He always does. I light every lamp on this street now. It doesn't keep him out. It only means I see whose window he's looking at.
* Have there been roses since? -> vallaki/black_roses:asks
* Goodnight, Ilie. -> END

# --- Evenings at the Blue Water Inn (their `hours`), and the stocks (data/schedule/vallaki.json) ---

~ goodwife_inn
Goodwife Marta [smile]: One cup of Urwin's red, and then home before the lamps are all lit. The Baron likes us in by dark. So does the dark.
-> END

~ carter_inn
Old Kolya: Sit, sit. This is the only chair in Vallaki nobody's ordered me to be cheerful in. I'm not giving it up.
-> END

~ grumbler
Anton the Cooper: Don't look at me like that. I smiled. I smiled the whole festival. Apparently it didn't reach my eyes.
* What happens now? -> grumbler_now
* Chin up. -> END

~ grumbler_now
Anton the Cooper: I stand here till the evening bell, then I go home and practise in the mirror. Third time this month. My wife says I've a face built for coopering, not for joy.
interject tag:kind: For what it's worth, it seems a perfectly good face.
* [if not quest.ribbons] Who told the Baron you weren't smiling? -> grumbler_who
* Chin up. -> END

~ grumbler_who
set ribbons_rumor
quest ribbons rumored
Anton the Cooper: Told? Nobody tells. There's a list. The girl with the ribbons writes down who won't wear one, and the next morning those are the faces in here. Ask her. Don't ask her where I can see; I'm in enough trouble.
-> END

# --- Lane 28 (2026-10-08): the town at work - the market row, the inn's porter, the square and the watch ---

~ herbwife
if flag.festival_over
Old Smaranda: Sage, garlic, wolfsbane. Same as always. The festival's done, so I can stop selling yellow ribbons too. Never liked yellow.
-> END
endif
Old Smaranda [smile]: Sage for sleep, garlic for the door, wolfsbane for the window. And a ribbon, dear, yellow, for your coat. They're watching who wears one.
* Why garlic for the door? -> herbwife_garlic
* Just looking. -> END

~ herbwife_garlic
Old Smaranda: Because the Baron says there's nothing to fear, and the Baron is always right. Garlic is two coppers a braid.
-> END

~ cloth_merchant
Master Costel [smile]: Bunting! Festival bunting, by the yard or the bolt! I have sold yellow to every house in Vallaki and three of them twice. Business has never been better, which worries me more than you'd think.
-> END

~ porter
Matei: Mind your feet! Sacks for Urwin, wine for the square, wicker for the sun. Everything in this town goes on my back sooner or later.
Matei: Heavy days are good days. You don't have time to think.
-> END

~ ribbon_girl
if flag.festival_over
Daciana: No more ribbons. Nobody's counting any more. I don't know what to do with my hands.
-> END
endif
if quest.ribbons and quest.ribbons != rumored
-> vallaki/ribbons:daciana
endif
Daciana [smile]: A ribbon for the festival! It's free. It's for the sun. Everybody wears one.
* Take a ribbon. -> ribbon_take
* No, thank you. -> ribbon_refuse
* [if flag.ribbons_rumor] Who wants to know, Daciana? -> vallaki/ribbons:who

~ ribbon_take
Narrator: She ties a yellow ribbon to your sleeve with quick, cold fingers, and the smile goes out of her eyes for a moment, with relief.
-> END

~ ribbon_refuse
Daciana: Oh. That's... I have to write that down. I'm sorry. It's not me who wants to know.
set ribbons_rumor
if not quest.ribbons
quest ribbons rumored
endif
-> END

~ sun_painter
Tudor: Third coat. The Baron says the sun must be brighter than the last one. The last one was very bright, and look where that got us.
-> END

~ patrol
Watchman Dobre: Keep moving, strangers. And smile. It's not a request. It's a festival.
-> END

~ raker
Gheorghe: Every morning I rake it smooth. Every afternoon the carts churn it up. Every morning I rake it smooth again. The Baron says this is what order looks like.
-> END

~ dog
Narrator: The big dog sniffs your boots for a long moment, decides you are not food and not trouble, and lies down across the square's best patch of sun.
-> END

